[{"page":1,"text":"Update #4 | August 21, 2026\n\nVineyard Regional Trail Enhancements\n\nLakeside Park and 400 South\n\nUpcoming Work Activities\n\nCrews have finished striping 400 South and the east entrance of Lakeside\n\nPark.\n\nThrough the month of August, crews will continue to install traffic poles,\ntraffic lights, and finish restoring landscaping.\n*Construction schedules are subject to change due to weather or other\nunforeseen circumstances.\n\nCenter Street and Holdaway Road\n\nUpcoming Work Activities\n\nCrews have poured the sidewalk on the southside of Center Street and\nHoldaway Road.","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"Through the month of August, crews will continue to restore ADA\npedestrian ramps and install signal poles.\n*Construction schedules are subject to change due to weather or other\nunforeseen circumstances.\n\nTraffic Alerts\n\nMotorists can expect intermittent lane closures on Center Street, Monday\nthrough Friday, 7 a.m. to 7 p.m., with weekend work as needed.\n\nActive transportation users (pedestrians, cyclists, etc.) will not be allowed\nin the construction areas.\n\nSchool Access\n\nKids walking to school can use their regular routes, as there are crossing\nguards to help kids cross 400 South safely.\n\nParents should talk with their kids about safe behaviors around\nconstruction and encourage them to avoid the work zone both during and\nafter work hours.\n\nSafety\n\nPlease encourage your children to avoid the construction area, both during\nand outside of work hours.\n\nLocal residents should exercise caution as they drive or walk through the\nconstruction zone. This is an active work zone, and conditions are\nconstantly changing.\n\nPlease pay attention to traffic control devices and instructions from crew\nmembers on-site. Remember to make eye contact with equipment\noperators before passing or crossing, to ensure they see you.","ocr":false},{"page":3,"text":"Questions or Concerns?\n\nEmail: claire.langford@consoreng.com\n\nHotline: 385-557-2586\n\nProject Background\n\nVineyard City and Orem City, in partnership with the Mountainland Association\nof Governments (MAG), are conducting a project to make several improvements\nto their pedestrian and active transportation systems.\nOne part of the project is the addition of a lighted/flashing warning signal, known\nas a Pedestrian Hybrid Beacon, to the Center Street crosswalk just west of\n\nFranklin Discovery Academy (see map below). This will make it easier for drivers\nto notice pedestrians waiting to cross, or actively crossing, the street at the\ncrosswalk.","ocr":false},{"page":4,"text":"The other piece of the project is to realign the 620 East and 400 South\nintersection, by moving the road entering the Lakeside Park parking lot slightly\nto the east (see map below). This also includes the installation of a traffic signal\nand crosswalks with updated road striping and signage.\n\nThis email is being sent by Consor on behalf of Vineyard City for the purposes of this project.\n\nVineyard City | 125 South Main Street | Vineyard, UT 84059 US\nUnsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice","ocr":false}]